t but it just shows you  they can't now the season's over they  can't they can't muzzle these guys if  they want to talk they're going to talk  and the failure here shireen in my  opinion was  that if they were going  to to lay down in this game they needed  to do a better job of signaling it to  everyone ahead of time make nate felt  the starter in that game that would have  been a better signal a point sims made  today on pft live when jim schwartz  comes out and says this is a no hat no  t-shirt game for us that says that  they're trying to win and maybe in  hindsight it was a middle finger by  schwartz who's walking away from the  eagles after this season and he's smart  enough to come up with something like  that where the message is going to get  through that hey we're trying to win  when they really weren't but the bottom  line is doug peterson failed and the  eagles organization failed to let people  inside or outside properly brace for  what ultimately happened  sound like the quarterbacks knew mike  and not many other players knew so it  obviously wasn't communicated well  but it doesn't matter what you think it  doesn't matter what i think about the  decision it doesn't matter what anyone  outside that locker room thinks it  doesn't matter what joe judge thinks all  that matters is what those players think  inside that locker room and we've heard  we've heard from miles sanders we've  heard the inside reports on how eagles  players feel about this this is a dark  cloud over this organization and they've  got a lot of repair work to do once they  come back into that building mike  because it's it's obvious that players  did not agree with this uh situation and  what doug peterson did or whoever made  the decision i i think it was probably  above doug peterson but whoever made the  decision  and i think that the repair work should  be happening now this isn't something  that should sit until april i remember  six years ago when the seahawks lost in  super bowl 49 on that fateful decision  to throw instead of run and the players  were up in arms about it you had some  players like bruce irvin immediately  speaking out about it and it was clear  that the players were upset i remember  pete carroll going on the today show and  i'm thinking why is he on the today show  well this is one way to communicate your  message because to the extent that you  have other family members of these  players who are watching the today show  and they see it and they understand  where pete carroll is coming from you  get other people in the family working  on you in a positive way to get you to  understand why i did what he did and i  think the eagles need to be plotting out  some sort of broader media strategy here  take but but see here's the problem  here's the problem they can never say  that they were trying to lose the game  the minute they do that is the minute  the nfl descends on  the eagles the way they descended on the  patriots for spygate one two and three  the way and deflategate and the way they  descended on the saints for bounty gate  you can't come out and say it the league  isn't going to do anything to you as  long as you keep your mouth shut that  you were trying to lose the minute you  say you were trying to lose you're dead  so i don't know what they can do here  shireen  yeah it's exactly right mike and they  went from ninth overall pick two to six  so we're all picked by losing and and i  i get it everybody get it gets it i  think why they did it but you know i  keep going back to travis kelsey's  comments from the middle of december and  even if you're out of it you play to win  and here's the reasons why you and it  was a great speech that he made  but  doug peterson and what that organization  did during that game basically spit in  the face of everything that travis  kelsey said uh in the middle of december  and so i don't know how you resolve that  with travis kelsey or other players  within that locker room because you said  they can't admit it so i'm not sure how  you do this repair work uh that the  seahawks were able to do and pete  carroll was able to do uh in the super  bowl when marshawn lynch didn't get the  ball and everyone on that team thought  marshawn lynch should have gotten the  ball  yeah because the problem is if you admit  it to enough players it's going to get  out that they're admitting it and that  could be enough to activate the league  office's disciplinary arm and you know  other teams in week 17 played to win  when it was in their best interest long  term to not play to win the vikings it  was in their best interest to lay down  against the lions it was in the lion's  best interest to lay down although the  interim coach doesn't care because he's  not going to be there anyway but there  are other examples of teams where you  could look at and say what like the  49ers i mean they were they tried to  beat the seahawks they don't benefit  from beating the seahawks kyle shanahan  is definitely going to be there next  year but teams played to win  in lesser platforms than that game  number 256 which has a a special vibe to  it  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

